#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Changelog {#changelog}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "[0.4.0] - 2026-09-22 {#040-2026-09-22}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Breaking changes**\n"
"- Renamed the input parameter `model` to `problem`.\n"
"- Renamed the output field `obj_value` to `objective_value`.\n"
"- Replaced the `postprocessing` option with `postprocessing_level`, which takes an integer in the range `[0, 3]` instead of a string. The previous values map to `\"off\"` -> `0`, `\"weak\"` -> `1`, `\"medium\"` -> `2`, and `\"strong\"` -> `3`, and the default is unchanged at `3`.\n"
"- Restructured `metadata.circuit_metrics`. It now reports `num_qubits`, `gate_count`, `depth`, `two_qubit_gate_count`, `two_qubit_gate_depth`, and `operations` separately for `before_transpilation` and `after_transpilation`, instead of a single flat dictionary of averaged gate counts. The field is `None` when the problem was solved during preprocessing and no circuit was run (error code `4712`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Features**\n"
"- Added the `seed_transpiler` option to make circuit synthesis and routing reproducible across runs.\n"
"- Added the `job_tags` option to attach your own tags to every Qiskit Runtime job the function submits.\n"
"- Added the output field `solution_bitstrings`, which returns the same solutions as `solutions` in bitstring form.\n"
"- Added `metadata.solver_info.variable_mapping`, which maps each variable name to its character position in the entries of `solution_bitstrings`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Documentation**\n"
"- Documented that continuous (real-valued) variables are not supported and that integer variables require explicit bounds. Such models fail with error code `4710`.\n"
msgstr ""

